statement:
Let $X$ be an integral scheme [def-pc-integral-scheme] with generic point $\eta$ and function field $k(X)=\mathcal O_{X,\eta}$, a field [def-sc-function-field], and let $\mathcal L$ be an invertible $\mathcal O_X$-module [def-sc-invertible-module]. For $x\in X$ write $\mathcal L_x$ for the stalk [def-weil-pbc-module-stalk], a module over $\mathcal O_{X,x}$, and $\lambda_x:\mathcal L_x\to\mathcal L_\eta$ for the map sending the germ at $x$ of a section $\sigma\in\mathcal L(W)$ ($W$ an open neighbourhood of $x$, which contains $\eta$) to its germ $\sigma_\eta$; for a nonempty open $U\subseteq X$ write $\lambda_U:\mathcal L(U)\to\mathcal L_\eta$, $\sigma\mapsto\sigma_\eta$. Regard $\mathcal O_{X,x}\subseteq k(X)$ through the injective germ map $\rho_x:\mathcal O_{X,x}\to k(X)$. Then:

1. for every $x\in X$ the $\mathcal O_{X,x}$-module $\mathcal L_x$ is free of rank one; in particular $\mathcal L_\eta$ is a $k(X)$-vector space of dimension one;
2. for every $x\in X$ the map $\lambda_x$ is injective, and if $e\in\mathcal L_x$ is a generator then $\lambda_x(e)$ is a $k(X)$-basis of $\mathcal L_\eta$ and $\lambda_x(\mathcal L_x)=\mathcal O_{X,x}\cdot\lambda_x(e)$;
3. for every nonempty open $U\subseteq X$ the map $\lambda_U$ is injective, and its image is the set of $\tau\in\mathcal L_\eta$ with $\tau\in\lambda_x(\mathcal L_x)$ for every $x\in U$.
